<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 66,529 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 66,529 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 66,529 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Tuesday compared to 56,520 tonnes in the same period on Monday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Tuesday     Jan 20</p>
<p>    Export cargo		 8,583	16,747</p>
<p>    Import cargo		57,946	39,773</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, two ships sailed and four berthed. In the next 24 hours, seven are expected to sail and eight are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Sugar		     7,500	 Faurei		21/1</p>
<p>Crude oil		70,000	 Stavros - 1	 21/1</p>
<p>High speed diesel    56,000	 Keefan		22/1</p>
<p>Kerosene/HSD	   27,300	 Chilham Castle    24/1</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
